Add option to keep workspace files out of the browser cache

This patch adds support for a new CLI flag called `--disable-file-cache`. When
set, workspace files are not stored on the client disk through two caches:

- The webview resource loader sends no ETag for a resource outside the
  webview's own extension, and the webview service worker only stores responses
  that have an ETag, so these resources stay out of Cache Storage.
- `/vscode-remote-resource` responds with `Cache-Control: no-store` for files
  outside the extension directories.

Extension resources keep their ETags so webviews still load extension code from
the cache. The default value for this is `false`.

To test, start code-server with `--disable-file-cache`, open a Markdown file
that embeds an image from the workspace, and open the preview. In the browser
dev tools, the `vscode-resource-cache-*` Cache Storage of the webview service
worker should have no entry for the image, and a request to
`/vscode-remote-resource?path=<image>` should respond with
`Cache-Control: no-store`.

